  },
  "hints": [
    "The complete range has a known sum.",
    "Subtract the actual array sum from the sum of 0 through n.",
    "Compute n*(n+1)//2 - sum(nums).",
    "The absent value can be zero or n, so both endpoints belong to the range."
  ],
  "editorial": "Because all input values are distinct and exactly one is absent, subtracting their sum from n(n+1)/2 cancels every present value and leaves the missing one. The sum formula must include n, not stop at n-1. The independent oracle constructs the full range as a set and takes the set difference.",
